{
	"info": {
		"name": "Emergency Ambulance Dispatch System",
		"description": "Full API test suite for the Emergency Ambulance Dispatch System backend.\n\nWorkflow (run folders in order):\n1. Base - health check\n2. Public - fetch seeded ambulance types & hospitals (captures IDs)\n3. Auth - register patient & driver, login admin (captures tokens)\n4. Admin - Infrastructure - create ambulance, hospital, manage drivers\n5. Patient - Create Request - create an emergency request\n6. Admin - Dispatch - priority change, assign ambulance, select hospital\n7. Driver - Complete Trip - accept, EN_ROUTE -> PICKED_UP -> HOSPITAL_ARRIVED -> COMPLETED\n8. Patient - Verify & Pay - history, notifications, cancel guard\n9. Payment - Stripe - create intent, confirm\n10. Admin - Dashboard & Reports\n11. Negative / RBAC Tests\n\nAuth: login/register return accessToken in data.accessToken; the collection auto-stores these into the variables adminToken / patientToken / driverToken and injects them via the Authorization header of each protected request.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "base_url", "value": "http://localhost:5000/api/v1" },
		{ "key": "adminToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "patientToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "driverToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "ambulanceTypeId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "hospitalId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "customHospitalId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "driverId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "ambulanceId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "requestId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "tripId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "notificationId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "paymentId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "clientSecret", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "paymentIntentId", "value": "" }
	],
